{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From Gilgal down to Bethel, from [Bb]Bethel down to the river
[F]The old prophet and his servant walked [C]the road together
[Bb]Stay here, the old man told him, but E[Dm]lisha would not stay
As [Bb]the LORD lives, I will not leave you, I [C]will walk with you today [Dm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
At the Jordan Elijah rolled his cloak and struck the [Bb]water
It [F]parted left and right, they crossed on the [C]dry ground
Ask what I may [Bb]do for you before I am taken [Dm]from you
Let me re[Bb]ceive a double portion of your [C]spirit
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]Suddenly a chariot of fire and horses of [Bb]fire appeared
And E[F]lijah went up to heaven in a [C]whirlwind
My [Bb]father, [Dm]my father
[Bb]The chariots [C]and horsemen of Is[Dm]rael
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [C] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Bb] | [C] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[C]And he [Bb]saw him no [C]more
He [Dm]picked up the cloak that had fallen
[Bb]He struck the river as [C]the old man had
And [Dm]the water parted for [C]him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
